## 5. Security / authorization

Method-level: **`@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")`** on `addOwner` (OwnerRestControllerV1.java line 122). `@roles` is the `Roles` bean (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/Roles.java`), `OWNER_ADMIN = "ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN"` (line 8) — so the caller needs authority `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`.

Enabled by **`BasicAuthenticationConfig`** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/BasicAuthenticationConfig.java`), `@EnableMethodSecurity(prePostEnabled = true)` (line 19), active only when `petclinic.security.enable=true` (line 20). Filter chain: CSRF disabled, `anyRequest().authenticated()`, HTTP Basic (lines 36-40); JDBC-backed users/roles (lines 45-54).

When `petclinic.security.enable=false` (the default in `src/main/resources/application.properties:49`), **`DisableSecurityConfig`** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/security/DisableSecurityConfig.java`) applies: `anyRequest().permitAll()` (line 25). Note `@EnableMethodSecurity` lives only on `BasicAuthenticationConfig`, so with security disabled the `@PreAuthorize` is not enforced.

