## Full ordered execution summary

1. `@Valid` on the interface validates `OwnerFieldsDto` (all `@NotNull/@Pattern/@Size/@Email` in section 2). Failure → 400 via `MethodArgumentNotValidException`.
2. `@PreAuthorize` role check `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (only enforced when security enabled).
3. Controller normalizes address (`AddressNormalizer`).
4. `OwnerFieldsValidator.findMissingFields` → 400 if any of firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone blank.
5. Map DTO→`Owner` (id/pets ignored → entity is "new").
6. `countOwnersByCity` ≥ 50 → 409 `CityCapacityExceededException`.
7. Resolve registration date (`RegistrationDatePolicy`); `countOwnersRegisteredOn` ≥ 100 → 429 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException`.
8. Normalize telephone (`TelephoneNormalizer`; invalid → 400 `InvalidTelephoneException`); `findOwnerByTelephone` non-empty → 409 `DuplicateTelephoneException`.
9. `findOwnersInHousehold`; if non-empty and not `sharesHousehold` → 409 `DuplicateHouseholdException`.
10. Set normalized telephone + email.
11. If `sharesHousehold`: `joinHousehold` assigns SHA-256 household id and back-fills existing members (extra `save` calls).
12. `saveOwner`: since new, generate `customerCode` (`CustomerCodeGenerator`, extra `countByCity`) and `namesakeCount` (`NamesakeCounter`, extra `findByLastNameIgnoreCase`), then `ownerRepository.save`.
13. JPA `@PrePersist resolveRegistrationDate` fires on insert.
14. Map entity→`OwnerDto` (computes displayName, membershipNumber, membershipTier, locality, initials); set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`; return **201 Created**.
